<article class="env-lemma" id="02K4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02K4">Lemma <span data-tag="02K4">29.35.16</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$, $g : Y \to S$ be morphisms of schemes. Assume $f$ is smooth. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to f^*\Omega _{Y/S} \to \Omega _{X/S} \to \Omega _{X/Y} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> (see Lemma <a href="/tag/01UX" data-tag="01UX">29.33.9</a>) is short exact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The algebraic version of this lemma is the following: Given ring maps $A \to B \to C$ with $B \to C$ smooth, then the sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to C \otimes _ B \Omega _{B/A} \to \Omega _{C/A} \to \Omega _{C/B} \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00RS" data-tag="00RS">10.131.7</a> is exact. This is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/04B2" data-tag="04B2">10.139.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>